--- OPES_TS ---

OPES (On-the-fly Probability Enhanced Sampling) metadynamics runs exploring the TS region of
the pph4 mechanism directly (as opposed to the harmonic-restraint umbrella sampling used in
../PMF_react_TS1/, ../PMF_react_TS2/ and ../US/). Each replica biases the angle/coordination
CVs 'aobpow' and 'cowbulkp' (see plumed_OPES_TS_repN.dat / plumed_pph4-hydrolysis.dat) with
PLUMED's OPES bias over a very long run (tens of millions of steps, restart snapshots every
100000 steps), letting the system freely explore the TS basin rather than pin it to a single
reaction-coordinate value. Output per replica: 'OPES_TS_repN.lammpstrj'/'.log', 'COLVAR'/
'Coord.info'/'OPES.log', 'KERNELS' (deposited OPES kernels), 'mg_coord.info' and
'model_devi.out' (NNP-committee deviation, QC), plus the full restart-snapshot series.

Five replicas (rep1..rep5) — one README covers all five, same protocol with different seeds.

Note: this README documents pre-existing content; no existing file was modified.
